{"html":"<article class=\"\"><div class=\"content-top\"><\/div><div class=\"textblock\" data-banner-type=\"no-banner\"><h1>Filter Accept List<span id=\"filter-accept-list\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#filter-accept-list\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h1><p style=\"color:inherit\">Filter Accept List. <\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Provides support for adding and removing devices from the Filter Accept List in the Bluetooth controller.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">The Filter Accept List allows filtering transmissions from other Bluetooth devices so that the local device only receives/accepts transmissions from the devices that it's interested in or wants to communicate with. Operations that support filtering provide a means to control how the Filter Accept List is used:<\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">For advertising, use the command <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/sl-bt-advertiser#sl-bt-advertiser-configure\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_bt_advertiser_configure<\/a> and <code>flags<\/code> bits <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/sl-bt-advertiser-flags#sl-bt-advertiser-use-filter-for-scan-requests\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">SL_BT_ADVERTISER_USE_FILTER_FOR_SCAN_REQUESTS<\/a> and <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/sl-bt-advertiser-flags#sl-bt-advertiser-use-filter-for-connection-requests\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">SL_BT_ADVERTISER_USE_FILTER_FOR_CONNECTION_REQUESTS<\/a> to control the advertising filter policy<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">For scanning, use the command <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/sl-bt-scanner#sl-bt-scanner-set-parameters-and-filter\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_bt_scanner_set_parameters_and_filter<\/a> to control the scanning filter policy <\/p><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"decl-class-section\"><h2>Functions<span id=\"func-declaration\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#func-declaration\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h2><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">sl_status_t<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#sl-bt-accept-list-add-device-by-bonding\">sl_bt_accept_list_add_device_by_bonding<\/a>(uint32_t bonding)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">sl_status_t<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#sl-bt-accept-list-add-device-by-address\">sl_bt_accept_list_add_device_by_address<\/a>(bd_addr address, uint8_t address_type)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">sl_status_t<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#sl-bt-accept-list-remove-device-by-bonding\">sl_bt_accept_list_remove_device_by_bonding<\/a>(uint32_t bonding)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">sl_status_t<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#sl-bt-accept-list-remove-device-by-address\">sl_bt_accept_list_remove_device_by_address<\/a>(bd_addr address, uint8_t address_type)<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">sl_status_t<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\"><a href=\"#sl-bt-accept-list-remove-all-devices\">sl_bt_accept_list_remove_all_devices<\/a>()<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"decl-class-section\"><h2>Macros<span id=\"define-declaration\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#define-declaration\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h2><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\">sl_bt_cmd_accept_list_add_device_by_bonding_id 0x005e0020<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\">sl_bt_cmd_accept_list_add_device_by_address_id 0x015e0020<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\">sl_bt_cmd_accept_list_remove_device_by_bonding_id 0x025e0020<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\">sl_bt_cmd_accept_list_remove_device_by_address_id 0x035e0020<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\">sl_bt_cmd_accept_list_remove_all_devices_id 0x045e0020<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\">sl_bt_rsp_accept_list_add_device_by_bonding_id 0x005e0020<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\">sl_bt_rsp_accept_list_add_device_by_address_id 0x015e0020<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\">sl_bt_rsp_accept_list_remove_device_by_bonding_id 0x025e0020<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\">sl_bt_rsp_accept_list_remove_device_by_address_id 0x035e0020<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div><div class=\"columns\"><div class=\"attributename has-text-right\">#define<\/div><div class=\"column\"><div class=\"attributename\">sl_bt_rsp_accept_list_remove_all_devices_id 0x045e0020<\/div><div class=\"classdescription\"><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"def-class-section\"><h2>Function Documentation<span id=\"func-definition\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#func-definition\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h2><div><h3>sl_bt_accept_list_add_device_by_bonding<span id=\"sl-bt-accept-list-add-device-by-bonding\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-bt-accept-list-add-device-by-bonding\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>sl_status_t sl_bt_accept_list_add_device_by_bonding (uint32_t bonding)<\/blockquote><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">bonding<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The bonding handle<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Add a device to the Filter Accept List based on its bonding handle.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">This command returns the error SL_STATUS_BT_CTRL_CONTROLLER_BUSY if the Filter Accept List is currently used by scanning filter policy, advertising filter policy, or by initiator filter policy, i.e. initiating connection to devices on the Filter Accept List. If the list is currently in use, the application needs to first stop the operation that uses the Filter Accept List, then add a device to the Filter Accept List, and then restart the operation that uses the Filter Accept List.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">SL_STATUS_OK if successful. Error code otherwise. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_bt_accept_list_add_device_by_address<span id=\"sl-bt-accept-list-add-device-by-address\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-bt-accept-list-add-device-by-address\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>sl_status_t sl_bt_accept_list_add_device_by_address (<a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/bd-addr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">bd_addr<\/a> address, uint8_t address_type)<\/blockquote><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/bd-addr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">bd_addr<\/a><\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">address<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Bluetooth address of the peer device <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint8_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">address_type<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enum <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/sl-bt-gap#sl-bt-gap-address-type-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_bt_gap_address_type_t<\/a>. The peer device address type. Values:<\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>sl_bt_gap_public_address (0x0):<\/strong> Public device address<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>sl_bt_gap_static_address (0x1):<\/strong> Static device address<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>sl_bt_gap_random_resolvable_address (0x2):<\/strong> Resolvable private random address<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>sl_bt_gap_random_nonresolvable_address (0x3):<\/strong> Non-resolvable private random address<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>sl_bt_gap_anonymous_address (0xff):<\/strong> Anonymous address. A Filter Accept List entry with this type matches all advertisements sent with no address.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Add a device to the Filter Accept List based on its identity address.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Use the special address type <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/sl-bt-gap#sl-bt-gap-anonymous-address\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_bt_gap_anonymous_address<\/a> to add an entry that matches all advertisements sent with no address.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">This command returns the error SL_STATUS_BT_CTRL_CONTROLLER_BUSY if the Filter Accept List is currently used by scanning filter policy, advertising filter policy, or by initiator filter policy, i.e. initiating connection to devices on the Filter Accept List. If the list is currently in use, the application needs to first stop the operation that uses the Filter Accept List, then add a device to the Filter Accept List, and then restart the operation that uses the Filter Accept List.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">SL_STATUS_OK if successful. Error code otherwise. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_bt_accept_list_remove_device_by_bonding<span id=\"sl-bt-accept-list-remove-device-by-bonding\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-bt-accept-list-remove-device-by-bonding\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>sl_status_t sl_bt_accept_list_remove_device_by_bonding (uint32_t bonding)<\/blockquote><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">bonding<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The bonding handle<\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Remove a device from the Filter Accept List based on its bonding handle.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">This command returns the error SL_STATUS_BT_CTRL_CONTROLLER_BUSY if the Filter Accept List is currently used by scanning filter policy, advertising filter policy, or by initiator filter policy, i.e. initiating connection to devices on the Filter Accept List. If the list is currently in use, the application needs to first stop the operation that uses the Filter Accept List, then remove a device from the Filter Accept List, and then restart the operation that uses the Filter Accept List.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">SL_STATUS_OK if successful. Error code otherwise. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_bt_accept_list_remove_device_by_address<span id=\"sl-bt-accept-list-remove-device-by-address\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-bt-accept-list-remove-device-by-address\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>sl_status_t sl_bt_accept_list_remove_device_by_address (<a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/bd-addr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">bd_addr<\/a> address, uint8_t address_type)<\/blockquote><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/bd-addr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">bd_addr<\/a><\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">address<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Bluetooth address of the peer device <\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint8_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">address_type<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enum <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/sl-bt-gap#sl-bt-gap-address-type-t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_bt_gap_address_type_t<\/a>. The peer device address type. Values:<\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>sl_bt_gap_public_address (0x0):<\/strong> Public device address<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>sl_bt_gap_static_address (0x1):<\/strong> Static device address<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>sl_bt_gap_random_resolvable_address (0x2):<\/strong> Resolvable private random address<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>sl_bt_gap_random_nonresolvable_address (0x3):<\/strong> Non-resolvable private random address<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>sl_bt_gap_anonymous_address (0xff):<\/strong> Anonymous address. A Filter Accept List entry with this type matches all advertisements sent with no address.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Remove a device from the Filter Accept List based on its identity address.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">Use the special address type <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/sl-bt-gap#sl-bt-gap-anonymous-address\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">sl_bt_gap_anonymous_address<\/a> to remove an entry that matches all advertisements sent with no address.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">This command returns the error SL_STATUS_BT_CTRL_CONTROLLER_BUSY if the Filter Accept List is currently used by scanning filter policy, advertising filter policy, or by initiator filter policy, i.e. initiating connection to devices on the Filter Accept List. If the list is currently in use, the application needs to first stop the operation that uses the Filter Accept List, then remove a device from the Filter Accept List, and then restart the operation that uses the Filter Accept List.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">SL_STATUS_OK if successful. Error code otherwise. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>sl_bt_accept_list_remove_all_devices<span id=\"sl-bt-accept-list-remove-all-devices\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#sl-bt-accept-list-remove-all-devices\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>sl_status_t sl_bt_accept_list_remove_all_devices ()<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Remove all devices from the Filter Accept List.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\">This command returns the error SL_STATUS_BT_CTRL_CONTROLLER_BUSY if the Filter Accept List is currently used by scanning filter policy, advertising filter policy, or by initiator filter policy, i.e. initiating connection to devices on the Filter Accept List. If the list is currently in use, the application needs to first stop the operation that uses the Filter Accept List, and then remove all devices from the Filter Accept List.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">SL_STATUS_OK if successful. Error code otherwise. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><\/div><div class=\"def-class-section\"><h2>&nbsp;<\/h2><div><\/div><div><\/div><div><\/div><div><\/div><div><\/div><div><\/div><div><\/div><div><\/div><div><\/div><div><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/article><footer class=\"footer-commons-msg\"><\/footer><div class=\"light_theme hidden-lg\" ub-in-page=\"634f96f53042a864e44b82f8\"><\/div><div class=\"dark_theme hidden-lg\" ub-in-page=\"6735652b86eaf07b7012c67e\"><\/div><div id=\"page-nav-buttons\" class=\"page-nav-buttons\"><\/div>","url":"http://docs.silabs.com/bluetooth/10.1.1/bluetooth-stack-api/sl-bt-accept-list","status":"success"}
